1461:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_eth.c **** *\*\param   pBuffer :
1462:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_eth.c **** *\*\          - Pointer on remote WakeUp Packet Filter Register buffer data (8 words).
1463:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_eth.c **** *\*\return  none
1464:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_eth.c **** *\*\note    When MAC RWK Packet Filter register is written, the content is transferred
1465:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_eth.c **** *\*\        from CSR clock domain to PHY receive clock domain after the write operation,
1466:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_eth.c **** *\*\        there should not be any further write to the MAC RWK Packet Filter register
1467:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_eth.c **** *\*\        until the first write is updated in PHY receive clock domain. Otherwise, the
1468:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_eth.c **** *\*\        second write operation does not get updated to the PHY receive clock domain.
1469:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_eth.c **** *\*\        Therefore, the delay between two writes to the MAC RWK Packet Filter register
1470:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_eth.c **** *\*\        should be at least 4 cycles of the PHY receive clock.
1471:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_eth.c **** **/
